From cde4de498e27bf503aa19264419bac6b862476c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chenhui Zhao <chenhui.zhao@nxp.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 19:45:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] xdp-trafficgen: fix ETF multi-stream CQ drain and startup
 races

- Add atomic trylock so children can also drain the shared CQ
- Re-sync CQ ring cache after fork() to prevent double-processing
- Create all stream contexts before forking (two-pass setup)
- Compute a common start time so all streams align
- Size UMEM per-stream (FRAMES_PER_STREAM) and pre-fault pages
- Add backoff sleep and needs_wakeup check to reduce CPU overhead
- Move parse_stream_config() to xdp-trafficgen.c with validation
- Extract run_stream_child(); increase MAX_STREAM_COUNT to 64

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Chenhui Zhao <chenhui.zhao@nxp.com>
---
